   "reason": "This collective labour agreement (PKB) sets company payroll rules that affect PPh 21 for permanent employees. It provides a tax allowance (gross-up) equal to the income tax due, with the company bearing the tax on bonuses. It fixes multiples of basic pay for THR, the 13th wage, leave allowances and long-leave compensation. It sets employer-paid JKK and JKM contributions as a percentage of basic pay, which enter gross income. It sets DPLK pension contributions for both employer and employee, which affect gross income and deductions. It also provides meal allowances in kind and severance and other termination payments.",
